From: Pavel Bragin <pabragin@yandex.ru>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: AN7563 ethernet fixes for the Xiaomi BE5000

Transmit:
- Queue frames asynchronously like the other SoCs. The AN7563 path
  busy-waited up to 1 ms per frame and cleared TX done queue entries a
  second time from xmit.
- Release a TX entry once: skip done reports for entries that are not in
  flight, clear DONE on release, and wait up to 20 us for a DONE bit that
  arrives after its report. A second release corrupted q->tx_list and lost
  an skb and its BQL completion, which stopped a netdev queue for good.
- Once a second, release TX entries the done queue never reported, when
  the ring has been idle for a whole second.

Frame engine:
- Stock PSE buffer setup: 1280 pages of 128 bytes, input queue reserves,
  share thresholds 500/480, CPU port flow control per port, MBI aging.
- Stall monitor: when the PSE input queues are full with RX DMA busy, or
  the PPE output queue stays stuck, recover in place: drop GDM ingress,
  stop NAPI and DMA, frame engine core reset, QDMA quick reset, program the
  rings again and restart. With RX DMA wedged no register write is safe,
  so the monitor reboots instead (airoha_eth.reboot_on_wedge).
- debugfs airoha_fe_stall: recoveries, PSE events, TX counters.

Shutdown and PPE:
- Drop GDM ingress and wait for QDMA idle on shutdown, stop the NPU, so a
  warm reboot does not loop.
- Do not bind bridged flows to local addresses.
- Replace a stale flow entry when a flowtable cookie is reused.
